cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use pyCOCOS in your work, please cite it as below.  The DOI is the
  Zenodo concept DOI: it resolves to the latest release, and every release
  also has its own version DOI on Zenodo.
type: software
title: pyCOCOS
abstract: >-
  Tokamak equilibria and magnetic coordinates in Python: g-EQDSK input and
  output in any COCOS convention, the magnetic field on the (R, z) grid, and
  flux-surface coordinates (Boozer, PEST, equal-arc, Hamada) with their
  metric and Jacobian.
authors:
  - given-names: Pablo
    family-names: Oyola
    affiliation: Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8455-1090"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23811057
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablo-oyola/pyCOCOS"
url: "https://pablo-oyola.github.io/pyCOCOS/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - plasma physics
  - tokamak
  - MHD equilibrium
  - COCOS
  - magnetic coordinates
  - Boozer coordinates
  - g-EQDSK
